Slots let one template receive content from another.

### Default and named slots

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    card = [:
        <h1>[$slot title]</h1>
        <section>[$slot]</section>
    ]

    [card:
        [$in title: Hello]
        Body content
    ]
]

The default and named forms are:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    [$slot]                 -- default slot
    [$slot name]            -- named slot
    [$in name: ...]         -- contribution to named slot
]

The default slot is declared with dollar-slot. A named slot is declared with
dollar-slot and a bare name. A named insert contributes with dollar-in
and the same name.

A slot occurrence can provide a compile-time String default, such as
`[$slot title = "Untitled"]` or `[$slot 1 = "Fallback"]`. Each occurrence
uses its own default only when no contribution is routed to that slot.
An explicitly empty contribution still suppresses the default. Multiple
named contributions concatenate in source order.

### Positional slots

Positive integer slots receive loose head contributions.

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    image = [:
        <img src="[$slot 1]" alt="[$slot]">
    ]

    [image, "logo.png": Site logo]
]

The first loose contribution fills slot `1`.

The remaining loose body content fills the default slot.

### Routing rules

- Loose contributions fill positional slots in ascending numeric order.
- Remaining loose contributions go to the default slot when one exists.
- Loose content that cannot be assigned is an error when no default slot exists.
- An unfilled slot without a default renders as an empty string.
- Repeated slots replay the same contribution.
- Named inserts target only their named slot.
- One application may combine named, positional and default contributions.

### Stored named inserts

Named inserts can be prepared in a binding and passed as loose contributions
through an immediate parent:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    card = [:
        <h1>[$slot title]</h1>
        [$slot]
    ]
    stored_title #= [$in title: Stored title]
    rendered #= [card: [stored_title] Body]
]

The stored helper is flattened into the immediate parent's slot-routing
stream. An insert with no matching immediate parent remains invalid.

### Runtime contributions

Runtime-capable templates support slot contributions from selected template
`if` branches and template loop bodies.

AST prepares the slot routing before HIR.

Runtime lowering appends the routed contributions through normal string
accumulators.

Unresolved slot or insert artefacts after routing are invalid template
structure.
